    {
      "question": "e-9480",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "89ddd3d6fba0e39016e207602ed364cbcd7e3bfd27b9e33c76f229bec5ff9379",
      "new_sha256": "d0a86fbfaa3a9e10c6144ffc246fdb97ecc9ecfc1a7a99506c5aacb3b5e7790b",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-9480",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9480.json",
          "file_sha256": "efe8a2abc6124505988cccaf6f3b434a86ae467fa061326175697412446e8653"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2607,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 2608
    },
    {
      "question": "e-9480",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "47c19dc92979015be081640fe4d7dc741f10b778b7fafa388baa9cb6d6df2112",
      "new_sha256": "7115f7b749a49e68f463c679512b61b4bffd905473bdd8e4605cd4666ad4066e",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-9480",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3\u0394{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j} & =\u0394{y}_{1}+\u0394{y}_{2}+\u0394{y}_{3}+\u22ef+\u0394{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+\u22ef+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+\u22ef+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9480.json",
          "file_sha256": "efe8a2abc6124505988cccaf6f3b434a86ae467fa061326175697412446e8653"
        }
      ],
